<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Basis bids steady to lower.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Basis bids steady to lower.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat were steady to lower Thursday at locations across the U.S. Plains as harvesting rolled on in northern Texas, grain merchandisers said.</p>
<p>While initial samples showed that the quality of the Texas crop was high, there was still a lack of information about quantity. Dealers complained that yield data about the new crop were not readily available.</p>
<p>&quot;In a year when yields are high, you start hearing about it right away,&quot; an Oklahoma dealer said. &quot;If you don't hear anything about yields, you can assume they're not too hot.&quot;  </p>
